From 43da6285156eaa60ebee632c26ab3ecefd58f808 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 14:32:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix false "already redeemed" status and add admin resolve for
 stuck payouts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

publicStatus() was collapsing both in-flight redemptions (redeeming) and
frozen ambiguous-failure redemptions (payout_unknown) into the same public
status as a completed redemption. A card whose payout genuinely failed or
was still in flight showed "This gift card has already been redeemed" on
the GiftLink page, even though the card had not actually been redeemed and
in the payout_unknown case may never resolve without human review.

- backend: split public status into distinct processing / on_hold values,
  leaving the raw internal status machine and the atomic claim path in
  /api/redeem completely untouched (no change to double-spend protection)
- backend: add resolveRedeemUnknown() + POST /api/admin/redeem/:id/resolve
  so a payout_unknown card can be released back to minted or confirmed as
  redeemed from the admin UI, instead of requiring direct DB access. Both
  outcomes use a conditional UPDATE ... WHERE status = 'payout_unknown' so
  a card can only be resolved once.
- frontend: GiftLink.jsx shows honest, distinct messaging for processing
  and on_hold instead of the redeemed message
- frontend: Admin.jsx adds RELEASE→MINTED / CONFIRM→REDEEMED buttons on
  payout_unknown rows in the cards table

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KvAh7hVc92EQaPsQ7zKfuN
